  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A ball is projected vertically from ground level, rising to a height of $25\\text{ m}$. It then bounces repeatedly, each time rising to a height of three fifths of the previous height. Find the total distance travelled by the ball up to the time when it hits the ground for the fourth time.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$108.8\\text{ m}$.\n\nCount four ground contacts and double the sum of the four flight heights.",
      "worked": "Taking the fourth bounce to mean the fourth ground contact, the four flight heights form a geometric sequence with first term $25$ and common ratio $\\frac35$. Each flight includes an ascent and a descent.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}D&=2\\left[25+25\\left(\\frac35\\right)+25\\left(\\frac35\\right)^2+25\\left(\\frac35\\right)^3\\right]\\\\D&=2\\times\\frac{25\\left[1-\\left(\\frac35\\right)^4\\right]}{1-\\frac35}\\\\D&=\\frac{544}{5}\\text{ m}\\\\D&=108.8\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
